        {
            "id": "a4336308-33e8-42f6-a5b9-bc4d80c039df",
            "build_id": "bef318f3-fbb0-459d-8312-d8f4f7962def",
            "round_number": 3,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-26T18:37:27.906209+00:00",
            "notes": "[Superflexor](item_580b77b4-0d63-469b-99a8-5372c55dfc1b) is a must-buy as Juno very easily gets full stacks with one use of her Primary Fire (so long as all five bullets hit). This paired up with the other abilities should get you a nice 20/20 split which with full stacks is more like a 20/45 split - which you will ideally have at (almost) all times.\nWith getting the Power [Stinger](item_e9d0d530-d620-4e74-a34d-38cdebfeb9a4) as well, most low health enemies should die so long as you hit them, even if they run behind cover. This allows you to essentially jiggle-peek the enemies, only coming out to hit them, wait out the DoT only to repeat the same pattern.\nIf you want your build to focus more on debuffing the enemies, I suggest you go with [Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98) next for the Slow effect, though [Catalytic Crystal](item_3e3f4f77-cdf8-4dda-a5b0-2fb9390aefc4) or [Lum\u00e9riCo Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) work also - especially if you need survivability without sacrificing [Ability Power](stat_ability_power).\nAs for the Power, if your team is doing fine on Survivability and Healing, I would go for [Cosmic Coolant](item_5584169d-94af-4efa-955c-263353a75553) to allow you to use your Torpedos more often. If the healing output is fine but the enemy team has a lot of Burst Damage, I suggest going for [Hyper Healer](item_108336b3-54d2-4d69-8ea4-c2da5affb7ca) as it works nicely with our [Ability Power](stat_ability_power) focused build already. If the healing output is severely lacking, definitetly go with [Medicinal Missiles](item_30eeab6c-4a1e-4a16-b9dd-e83d633caa40) as you will function as a sort of mini-Ana for your team, able to boost all healing for 3s.",
